libstdc++ 13 <memory_resource>: the bodies of __normal_iterator's operator++,
operator--, operator+ and operator- (bits/stl_iterator.h:1117-1342) are
dropped for __normal_iterator<__pool_resource::_BigBlock *, ...> ("pointer
arithmetic with unknown object size": vector<_BigBlock> is a member of
__pool_resource while _BigBlock is incomplete, [vector.overview]/4), and
polymorphic_allocator::destroy (bits/memory_resource.h:502, "member
operator got incomplete type on left hand side").  Being reduced; a
header-free imitation passes.  g++ 13 accepts this program, and it fails
only its WRONG assertion.
